# Entrega (fonte oficial)

This is the official delivery architecture. Seeds, migrations, refactors, deploys, and new features must not replace it. If a new feature conflicts, the feature adapts to this rule.

1. Coverage = point inside the green polygon. Outside = "Não entregamos nesta região."
2. Fee = KM tier table from store to that point. Never area `minFee`/`feePerKm` when tiers exist.
3. Typed address, GPS, and map pin all call `applyCoordinates` → `validateDeliveryCoverage(lat, lng)`. Same point, same result.
4. Bairros has a persisted master switch `km_delivery_config.neighborhoods_enabled`. Off = ignore every neighborhood fee; delivery is store + green polygon + KM only. On = neighborhood fees may run only when áreas and KM are not the coverage owner. Seed/migration/deploy must never UPDATE this flag (ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS only; first insert default false). The only writer is PUT `/admin/delivery-zones/settings`.
5. Do not re-insert `DEFAULT_DELIVERY_ZONES`. Do not delete saved neighborhoods on boot. Cadastro stays; the switch decides if it is used.
6. Do not geocode to a namesake in another neighborhood (Portão vs Itinga) or to Lauro city centroid. Unmapped real streets: GPS or map pin.
7. Street registry cannot overwrite an allowed polygon/KM result.

Keep `scripts/gps-delivery-coverage-selftest.mjs`, `scripts/delivery-areas-resolve-selftest.mjs`, and `scripts/neighborhoods-toggle-selftest.mjs` passing.
